; Exactly one diagnostic. Empty path is the index pass's convention —
; it walks outside path tracking, and its two older diagnostics
; (`duplicate_cross_ref_target`, `cyclic_cross_ref`) anchor on span
; alone for the same reason.
;
; The absence of `not_cross_ref` here is the assertion, not an omission:
; `u_time` would have resolved and `u_res` would not, and neither is
; reported, because a poisoned bucket has no answer to give.
(diagnostics
  (diagnostic :code cross_ref_extraction_failed :path []))
